Hi Jan.

There is actually an "unsupported" version of the CDF file available  
from Affy at:
http://www.affymetrix.com/support/technical/libraryfilesmain.affx

AFAIK, Bioconductor does not provide CDF environments for these chips.

One option is to build the environments yourself, e.g. the oligo/ 
pdInfoBuilder route:
http://article.gmane.org/gmane.science.biology.informatics.conductor/18963/

Another option is to use the aroma.affymetrix R package:
http://groups.google.com/group/aroma-affymetrix/

... within that, there is a CDF file available from:
http://groups.google.com/group/aroma-affymetrix/web/ragene-1-0-st-v1

... and yet another R package you could try is 'xps':
http://article.gmane.org/gmane.science.biology.informatics.conductor/17839/

Cheers,
Mark




